Changelog: 27-10-2026 20:04:40

Fixed. The window answers faster, on Windows most of all (owner, 27-10-2026: it was slow there, where starting a
git process takes some 20 ms): reading the checkout started about 230 git processes, one after the other, on the
window's own thread; now about 75, eight at a time. The tags and the new files are read once instead of once per
app, the check for tags made before their bump reads every VERSION with one git cat-file, and so does step 1 for
the CHANGELOGs at the last tags. A Refresh on Windows takes under a second instead of about four; the answers are
the same.

Fixed. On Windows, step 1's suggested versions counted CHANGELOG entries as new that were not: git's output was read
in Windows' own encoding, which garbled every é and × of a CHANGELOG read at a tag, so none of its entries matched
the current file. It is read as UTF-8 now, as on Linux.

